      "content": "Absolutely not, baby aspirin is dangerous for children under 19 because it can cause Reye's syndrome, a life-threatening condition that causes brain swelling and liver failure. You should never give aspirin to a child with a fever, especially one who is already lethargic, as this masks symptoms and delays proper treatment. Instead, give your child acetaminophen or ibuprofen at the correct pediatric dosage based on their weight, and call your pediatrician immediately to discuss the lethargy.",
